3	michael jackson	3fMbdgg4jU18AjLCKBhRSm	https://i.scdn.co/image/ab6761610000e5eb997cc9a4aec335d46c9481fd	Michael Jackson, often referred to as the 'King of Pop,' revolutionized the music industry with his innovative dance moves, including the moonwalk, and groundbreaking music videos like 'Thriller.' His album 'Thriller' remains the best-selling album of all time, and he won numerous awards, including 13 Grammy Awards. Jackson's influence extends beyond music, impacting fashion, dance, and popular culture globally.	f
4	madonna	6tbjWDEIzxoDsBA1FuhfPW	https://i.scdn.co/image/ab6761610000e5eb6ccc1215f5b205aa6b34b48b	Madonna, known as the 'Queen of Pop,' has continuously reinvented her music and image throughout her career, influencing pop culture and fashion. She has sold over 300 million records worldwide and is recognized for hits like 'Like a Virgin' and 'Material Girl.' Madonna's impact on the music industry includes her advocacy for social issues and her ability to remain relevant across decades.	f
5	the police	5NGO30tJxFlKixkPSgXcFE	https://i.scdn.co/image/1f73a61faca2942cd5ea29c2143184db8645f0b3	The Police, formed by Sting, Stewart Copeland, and Andy Summers, blended rock, reggae, and jazz, creating a unique sound that influenced many bands. Their hits like 'Every Breath You Take' and 'Roxanne' are iconic. The band won six Grammy Awards and was inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame in 2003, cementing their legacy in music history.	f
