COPY public.track (id, track_name, spotify_track_id, album_name, album_artwork, year_released, is_explicit, duration_ms, popularity, artist_id, featured_artist_id, artist_display_name, mode_flag, detail, created_at) FROM stdin;
1	forever and ever amen	1ipcb9qXpSHWhSUvdxJhsx	Always & Forever	https://i.scdn.co/image/ab67616d0000b273723376f081b369b02795a7fb	1987	f	212640	79	1	\N	Randy Travis	SOLO	Now, let's take a stroll down memory lane with Randy Travis's 'Forever and Ever Amen.' This gem was penned by the talented Paul Overstreet and Don Schlitz, who wove a tapestry of love and commitment that resonated deeply with fans. Did you know that the song's iconic steel guitar was played by none other than Paul Franklin, adding that extra layer of warmth to the track? It soared to the top of the charts, staying there for three weeks, a testament to its universal appeal. And here's a fun fact: during recording sessions, Randy insisted on doing multiple takes to get the emotion just right, showcasing his dedication to his craft. So, from all of us here, keep those love songs spinning, and remember, you're always number one with us!	2025-07-28 09:41:36.974847
2	the chair	4sDiJmHNcm0wLTH8ns65va	Something Special	https://i.scdn.co/image/ab67616d0000b273bdd3a744197aeb8fe477e63d	1984	f	170906	63	2	\N	George Strait	SOLO	Let's cozy up with George Strait's 'The Chair,' a song that's as smooth as a velvet curtain. Written by the brilliant Hank Cochran and Dean Dillon, this track tells a story that unfolds like a classic film. The recording took place at the legendary Sound Emporium Studio in Nashville, where the magic of the music industry often happens. Did you know that George chose to record it in one take, capturing the raw emotion and charm that made it a hit? It climbed to the top of the country charts, proving once again that storytelling in music is timeless. And here's a little behind-the-scenes tidbit: the song's producer, Jimmy Bowen, added subtle strings to enhance the cinematic feel. So, keep your radio tuned right here, where the hits just keep on coming!	2025-07-28 09:41:36.974847
3	billie jean	7J1uxwnxfQLu4APicE5Rnj	Thriller	https://i.scdn.co/image/ab67616d0000b273de437d960dda1ac0a3586d97	1983	f	294226	85	3	\N	Michael Jackson	SOLO	Now, let's dive into the magic behind 'Billie Jean'. Did you know that Michael Jackson wrote this song in his bedroom? That's right, the King of Pop was inspired by a fan letter claiming he was the father of a woman's child. Talk about drama! The song's iconic bassline was played by Louis Johnson, who used a custom Yamaha bass guitar. And here's a fun fact: during recording, Michael insisted on keeping the squeaky floor sound in the intro because he loved its unique vibe. And there you have it, folks, a true masterpiece born from personal stories and studio magic. Keep your dial locked right here for more musical tales!	2025-07-28 16:32:29.568332
4	like a virgin	1ZPlNanZsJSPK5h9YZZFbZ	Like a Virgin	https://i.scdn.co/image/ab67616d0000b27399d424b0873a9a714279a9f3	1984	f	218626	73	4	\N	Madonna	SOLO	Alright, let's talk about 'Like a Virgin'. Madonna's hit was co-written by Tom Kelly and Billy Steinberg, who initially thought it was too risqué. But Madonna saw its potential and made it her own. The song was recorded at Sigma Sound Studios in New York, where the team used a LinnDrum machine to create that catchy beat. And get this: during the video shoot in Venice, Madonna nearly drowned in a gondola! Now that's dedication to her craft. So, from a daring video to a bold song, 'Like a Virgin' broke boundaries and became an anthem. Stay tuned for more behind-the-scenes stories!	2025-07-28 16:32:29.568332
5	every breath you take	1JSTJqkT5qHq8MDJnJbRE1	Synchronicity (Remastered 2003)	https://i.scdn.co/image/ab67616d0000b273c8e97cafeb2acb85b21a777e	1983	f	253920	92	5	\N	The Police	SOLO	Let's take a closer look at 'Every Breath You Take'. This classic was penned by Sting during a tumultuous time in his life, and it's said he wrote the lyrics in just one afternoon. The song was recorded at AIR Studios in Montserrat, where the serene environment helped shape its haunting melody. Fun fact: the iconic guitar riff was played by Andy Summers on a 1961 Fender Telecaster. And here's a bit of trivia: this song was the biggest-selling single of 1983 in the UK. From personal struggles to chart-topping success, 'Every Breath You Take' is a testament to the power of music. Keep it right here for more fascinating stories!	2025-07-28 16:32:29.568332
6	i love rock n roll	2Cdvbe2G4hZsnhNMKyGrie	I Love Rock 'N' Roll (Expanded Edition)	https://i.scdn.co/image/ab67616d0000b2733c73b2e0a6aa490736f19751	1981	f	175173	81	6	\N	Joan Jett & the Blackhearts	SOLO	Now, let's rock out with 'I Love Rock 'N' Roll'. Joan Jett and the Blackhearts made this song their own, but did you know it was originally written by Alan Merrill and Jake Hooker of the Arrows? Joan heard it on a trip to England and knew she had to record it. The track was produced at the legendary Chappell Studios in London, where Joan played rhythm guitar herself. And here's a cool fact: the song spent seven weeks at the top of the Billboard Hot 100. From its British origins to American rock stardom, 'I Love Rock 'N' Roll' is a true classic. Stay tuned for more rockin' tales!	2025-07-28 16:32:29.568332
7	endless love	0rt0dZ11FVsvprbarag5tk	Back To Front	https://i.scdn.co/image/ab67616d0000b273062abeae9a2643960ba40f35	1981	f	268293	60	7	\N	Lionel Richie and Diana Ross	DUET	Let's get into the romance of 'Endless Love'. This duet was co-written by Lionel Richie, who crafted the lyrics with his wife Brenda in mind. The song was recorded at Kendun Recorders in Burbank, where Lionel and Diana Ross's voices blended perfectly. Did you know that the song's lush orchestration was arranged by Gene Page, who used a full string section to create that dreamy sound? And here's a sweet fact: 'Endless Love' spent nine weeks at number one on the Billboard Hot 100. From heartfelt lyrics to chart-topping success, this song is a timeless love ballad. Keep your radio on for more musical love stories!	2025-07-28 16:32:29.568332
\.


