COPY public.track_ranking (id, track_id, decade_genre_id, tracklist_id, ranking, intro, created_at) FROM stdin;
2	1	1	1	1	Kicking off the 1980s country charts at number one, 'Forever and Ever Amen' by Randy Travis from the album Always & Forever is a timeless classic that promises eternal love!	2025-07-28 00:00:00
3	2	1	1	2	At number two in the 1980s, George Strait's 'The Chair' from the album Something Special sits comfortably, weaving a tale of romance with a touch of mystery.	2025-07-28 00:00:00
4	3	2	1	1	Ranked #1 in the 1980s, 'Billie Jean' by Michael Jackson from the album Thriller is a pop masterpiece that still gets everyone on their feet!	2025-07-28 00:00:00
5	4	2	1	2	Madonna's 'Like a Virgin' hit #2 in the 1980s pop charts. From the album Like a Virgin, it's a bold anthem that defined an era.	2025-07-28 00:00:00
6	5	2	1	3	Did you know? 'Every Breath You Take' by The Police, from Synchronicity (Remastered 2003), clinched the #3 spot in the 1980s pop rankings!	2025-07-28 00:00:00
7	6	2	1	4	Joan Jett and The Blackhearts rocked the 1980s with 'I Love Rock 'N' Roll', securing #4 in pop. It's from the album I Love Rock 'N' Roll (Expanded Edition).	2025-07-28 00:00:00
8	7	2	1	5	Lionel Richie's 'Endless Love' soared to #5 in the 1980s pop scene. From the album Back To Front, it's a timeless duet that melts hearts.	2025-07-28 00:00:00
\.


